Spoilers!!!

After blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail and +2 Stormbringer:

I would say a blessed amulet of life saving is a must. No matter how
good you think you are, something always comes along to stuff you up,
e.g: a nymph steals you're speed boots and gloves, then the wizard
reappears with his brood, which includes a cockatrice, and
  you slow down -more-
  you are turning to stone -etc etc-
  But wait, your medallion begins to glow ;-)

In my opinion, speed boots are better than any gloves, so wish for them.
If you have magic resistance (via gray dragon mail), a cloak of
displacement is excellent value. Further on the armor side of things,
a shield of reflection is useful for protecting you scrolls and potions
from the (not infrequent) blasts of fire or frost you sustain from 
dragons, hell hounds and winter wolves.

If you don't have teleport control, then a ring of teleport control is
vital (I am assuming you at least have teleport). A ring of levitation
is also very useful if you currently have no means of levetating.

If you are a bit low in the hit point department, 3 cursed scrolls of
genocide are very handy.

More spoilers (wishing hints)!!!

  * when you wish for your scroll of charging, make it 3 blessed scrolls
    of charging. You can then recharge your favourite wand, magic marker
    and/or magic lamp as well.

  * I prefer wishing for +2 blessings on weapons and armor rather than
    +3, since +3 seems to fail about half the time and I end up with +0.
    Just my opinion though.

  * If you are prepared to wait, a wand of polymorph my be a better use
    of a wish than dragon mail, since you can make dragon mail, and then
    still use the wand. You can also recharge it again with one of your
    scrolls.

Happy wishing!
